  <section id="en" lang="en" hidden>
    <p>Lee Seokhee (the “Developer”) respects the privacy of users of RoteCat (package name: <strong>app.rotecat</strong>, the “App”). This policy explains what information the App processes and why.</p>

    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Important Accessibility Service Disclosure</strong><br>
      The App uses an Accessibility Service to determine whether a regular YouTube video has entered full screen and to change the screen orientation automatically. It operates only after the user turns on the feature in the App and grants accessibility access. Information observed through the service is processed immediately and locally on the device and is not sent to the Developer's servers or advertising providers.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Information processed by the App</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Accessibility events:</strong> The App observes the current app/window and the structure and bounds of YouTube interface elements to determine whether a regular video is full screen and to exclude Shorts from rotation.</li>
      <li><strong>Device orientation:</strong> The physical device orientation and current display orientation are checked temporarily to select the appropriate landscape direction.</li>
      <li><strong>On-device settings:</strong> The App stores its enabled state, widget cooldown state, and the previous auto-rotate setting and rotation value needed for recovery.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising information:</strong> When ads are provided in the free version, the Google Mobile Ads SDK may process advertising identifiers, IP address, approximate location, device and app information, ad interactions, and diagnostics.</li>
      <li><strong>Purchase information:</strong> Google Play processes payments for the ad-removal product. The App may process a product identifier and purchase status to remove ads and restore purchases. The Developer does not directly collect payment card or bank account details.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The App is not designed to collect text you type, passwords, messages, video content, or web browsing history through the Accessibility Service, and it does not store or transmit such information to the Developer's servers.</p>

    <h2>2. Purposes of processing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Detect entering and leaving full screen for regular YouTube videos</li>
      <li>Change screen orientation and restore the previous rotation settings</li>
      <li>Provide the home-screen widget and user preferences</li>
      <li>Display ads, manage consent, and process or restore ad-removal purchases</li>
      <li>Prevent errors, maintain security, and improve the service</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Permissions and sensitive APIs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Accessibility Service:</strong> Identifies YouTube full-screen state and Shorts locally on the device.</li>
      <li><strong>Modify system settings:</strong> Changes auto-rotate and display orientation and restores the previous settings when the feature ends.</li>
      <li><strong>Internet and network access:</strong> May be used for advertising, consent management, and Google Play Billing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The Accessibility Service is not presented as an accessibility aid and is used only for the screen-rotation automation described above.</p>

    <h2>4. Third-party services and sharing</h2>
    <p>The App may use Google AdMob, Google User Messaging Platform (UMP), and Google Play Billing for advertising and payments. Google may process information under its own privacy policy.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information for advertising</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>The Developer does not sell personal information. Screen information observed by the Accessibility Service is not used for ad personalization or shared with advertising providers. Personal information is not disclosed to third parties except when reasonably necessary to comply with law, protect users, or maintain security.</p>

    <h2>5. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>App preferences and rotation recovery information remain on the user's device and can be deleted by clearing the App's data or uninstalling the App. Information processed by advertising and payment providers is retained and deleted under their respective policies. The App does not create a user account, so the Developer does not retain account information.</p>

    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>The Developer limits processing to what is necessary and keeps accessibility and orientation analysis on the device wherever possible. However, no electronic processing method can guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>The App is not directed to children, and the Developer does not knowingly collect personal information from children. If such collection becomes known, reasonable steps will be taken promptly.</p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when the App's features, SDKs, or legal requirements change. Material changes will be announced through the App or this page, and the effective date will be updated.</p>

